    n<// The recording macros assist users who implement the <uvm_object::do_record>> u<582> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3624> s<583> f<10> l<25:1> el<25:79>
    n<// method. They help ensure that the fields are recorded using a vendor-> u<583> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3624> s<584> f<10> l<26:1> el<26:73>
    n<// independent API. Unlike the <uvm_recorder> policy, fields recorded using> u<584> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3624> s<585> f<10> l<27:1> el<27:76>
    n<// the macros do not lose type information--they are passed> u<585> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3624> s<586> f<10> l<28:1> el<28:60>
    n<// directly to the vendor-specific API. This results in more efficient recording> u<586> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3624> s<587> f<10> l<29:1> el<29:81>
    n<// and no artificial limit on bit-widths. See your simulator vendor's > u<587> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3624> s<588> f<10> l<30:1> el<30:71>
    n<// documentation for more information on its transaction recording capabilities.> u<588> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<3624> s<589> f<10> l<31:1> el<31:81>
